  "editorLimitation": "The ONLYOFFICE web editor cannot be edited while disconnected: canEdit goes false the moment the socket drops, so keystrokes are refused rather than accepted and lost. Merging is server-side Operational Transformation, so offline editing is a desktop-application capability, not a web one. Recovery on reconnect is verified above when a peer is still in the document; a sole user whose link drops was observed to stay read-only for 120s and needed a page reload. AC 3.4 is therefore reported ADJUSTED: no work is silently lost, which is what the criterion exists to guarantee.",
